<interrogationes unitas="quadrans">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I draw an image in a terminal with quadrant block characters?
    <responsum symbolum="quadrans_optiones_ordinariae quadrans_mensurare quadrans_computare QuadransCellula" via="lib/tessellatio.c">Take
      quadrans_optiones_ordinariae (quadrants, MEDIA colours, black
      fundus), ask quadrans_mensurare how many cells the pixel region
      needs, allocate that many QuadransCellula yourself, then call
      quadrans_computare. Each cell gives a runa (a codepoint, not a
      UTF-8 string) and two 0x00RRGGBB colours, foreground and
      background, in row order. tessellatio scales its pixel layer to
      columns * 2 by lines * 2 pixels with imago_scalare and then calls
      quadrans_computare, which yields exactly one cell per terminal
      cell.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I size an image so it fits a cell area without looking stretched?
    <responsum symbolum="quadrans_aptare QuadransModus" via="tessera/instrumenta/principalia/effigies.c">quadrans_aptare(img_lat,
      img_alt, max_lat, max_alt, modus, aspectus, &amp;sub_lat,
      &amp;sub_alt) gives the pixel size to scale the image to (up or
      down), keeping its proportions for a cell whose width / height is
      aspectus hundredths (QUADRANS_ASPECTUS_ORDINARIUS is L, i.e. 1:2).
      It does not scale anything: resize the image yourself (the
      effigies viewer uses imago_scalare with IMAGO_SCALA_AREA) and
      then call quadrans_computare. Any zero input gives 0 x 0.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I get exact colours instead of two colours per 2x2 block?
    <responsum symbolum="QuadransModus quadrans_computare" via="lib/quadrans.phase-log.md">Yes,
      with modus QUADRANS_DIMIDIUM: each cell is 1x2 pixels, the top
      pixel is the foreground under U+2580 and the bottom the
      background, so colours are exact but horizontal resolution is
      halved. Measured on two photographs at the same terminal size
      (phase-log Q3) the quadrant mode had 3.8 and 7.3 times less error
      than half-blocks, which is why quadrants are the default.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why is MEDIA the default colouring rather than the extreme pair OpenTUI uses?
    <responsum symbolum="quadrans_optiones_ordinariae QuadransColores quadrans_error" via="lib/quadrans.phase-log.md probationes/fixa/quadrans/aurum_errores.txt">For
      a fixed split of the four pixels the mean of each group minimises
      the squared error, so QUADRANS_MEDIA is never worse than
      QUADRANS_EXTREMA, which uses the same split. quadrans_error
      measured MEDIA at about 46% of EXTREMA's error on the
      photographs; the numbers are a ratchet in aurum_errores.txt.
      Whether EXTREMA looks sharper is a matter of taste, so it stays
      selectable.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what does quadrans do with transparent pixels and pixels outside the image?
    <responsum symbolum="quadrans_computare QuadransOptiones">Both
      become QuadransOptiones.fundus. Alpha is composited against
      fundus FIRST, because terminal cells have no alpha, and pixels
      outside the image or past the region (an odd width or height, a
      region partly off the image) read as fundus. A NIHIL imago gives
      cells that are all fundus. Set fundus to the terminal background
      colour, as tessellatio does.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why does a block of four equal pixels come out as a space instead of a full block?
    <responsum symbolum="quadrans_computare QuadransCellula">A
      uniform block (and in half-block mode two equal pixels) becomes
      U+0020 with that colour as the background, because a glyph drawn
      by the terminal font can leave a visible seam where a space with
      a background colour cannot. So runa 0x2588 never appears; a
      space cell carries its colour in color_fundi (color_litterae is
      the same value).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I measure how faithful a quadrant rendering is?
    <responsum symbolum="quadrans_error quadrans_computare">quadrans_error
      takes the same image, region and options plus the cells
      quadrans_computare produced, rebuilds the pixels from each cell's
      pattern and returns the mean squared error per channel in
      hundredths (0 is perfect, an empty region is 0). Passing cells
      computed with different options or a different region gives a
      meaningless number; nothing checks it.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can quadrans allocate the output or keep state between frames?
    <responsum symbolum="quadrans_computare quadrans_mensurare" via="include/quadrans.h">No,
      by design it is pure: no allocation, no state, and it depends only
      on latina.h and imago_typus.h, so tessera, the terminal emulator
      and a window can share it. The caller provides the
      QuadransCellula array sized by quadrans_mensurare, and turns runa
      into UTF-8 and colours into its own cell format.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
